  on buying a side or a salad when i know  that i've got the ingredients  in my fridge to throw something together  super fast  so what do i do i have both this can  save me a lot of money since  i often find that salads from some  restaurants that aren't actual salad  restaurants  they're kind of meh and they're also  usually super overpriced  but putting a bowl of like steamed  vegetables or salad  or some rice or bread on the table just  helps make for a more  balanced satisfying meal are you team  rice or team noodle i am definitely a  noodle girl but i love me  some progress  next know that not all your takeaway  meals need to be  perfectly balanced in fact i would say  at least  for me half the time mine are like just  straight up carbs  and i'm okay with that i know that in a  lot of my reviews you see me critique  individual meals but i do that so that  you have  ideas on how to make that particular  meal or meal like that  more satiating and more balanced in the  real world  it wouldn't matter if you had zero  vegetables at dinner other than i guess  like tomato sauce  on pizza or that it's low in protein  because you just wanted  straight up carbs that's how i roll like  all the time  and i have zero shame in that but i also  know  that if i look at the big picture it  will all balance itself out  i know that i probably had some salad  for lunch or  fruit as a snack with some beans or eggs  or fish or chicken in the day there for  protein  and the next day i'm probably gonna  start my day with yogurt and fruit  because  if i'm listening to my body i usually do  wake up after a  salty rich meal craving something  fresh so ultimately trust your body and  don't be so hard on yourself if the  macros are not perfect  at every meal and finally don't freak  out if the meal  doesn't live up to the hype i think when  we limit our consumption of  fun foods to just like a cheat day or a  cheat meal we put an enormous amount of  stock  into everything that we eat we might be  nervous to try something new because  we're worried it won't live up to like  our cheat day standards  or we feel deeply disappointed  when something arrives that maybe is not  what we were expecting  or ordered repeat after me tomorrow  is another delicious day not all meals  are going to be home runs and that goes  for homemade ones too  now i get that there's added  disappointment when you've spent good  money on something so  sometimes i do try to doctor something  up by adding like a sauce or some kind  of seasoning  if i think it's salvageable but  sometimes you just gotta say  hey you know what it filled my belly it  did  its job next time i'll order something  else  and that my friends is how you support  your local restaurant industry when it's  financially feasible to you  and also help make your life easier and  more fun  without unnecessary anxiety around  restaurant food  so a big thank you again to magic spoon  for sponsoring  if you like this video be sure to give  it the thumbs up leave me a comment  below with your  go-to take out food what do you love to  order i want to know if you're in  toronto let me know where i should be  ordering from and  definitely check out the list below in  some of my favorite restaurants  don't forget to subscribe to the channel  and i will see you next time on abby's  kitchen  bye

